{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-lie-bracket","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:categorical-q-lie-bracket","kind":"definition","title":"Categorical $q$-Lie bracket","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter"],"tags":["lie-bracket","deformation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket","text":"categorical-q-lie-bracket.md","leanSource":"categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:categorical-q-lie-bracket\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed Lie bracket</strong> on derivations of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  [X, Y]_q =  q^{-1}[X, Y] + (1 - q^{-1})\\bigl(\\varTheta_A(X)[\\xi, Y] - \\varTheta_A(Y)[\\xi, X]\\bigr),</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varTheta_A</code> is the canonical <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>-form dual to the Reeb derivation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.md","heading":"Definition","number":"4.19.2","page":"b/def-categorical-q-lie-bracket","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":55},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
